                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/pulls/comments/4478829013"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think we can keep this condition broader. C `int` -> `long` coercion is fine, for example. Only coercions that change the value type are critical, and there only seems to be int->float->complex which poses problems.\n\nWe might want to fix this directly in `PyrexTypes.reduce_spanning_types()`. If the result is a C float or complex type, we can look at the original types to see if their values would change with the spanning type, and fall back to `object` if so.",
            "commit_id": "9ba7db36bdd4c7046211de0ee6f251dcc4f7e47d",
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2026-11-05T09:40:11Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -186,21 +186,25 @@ def infer_sequence_item_type(env, seq_node, index_node=None, seq_type=None):\n         if None in item_types or py_object_type in item_types:\n             # Could not infer all (starred) types to specific types.\n             return None\n-        item_type = PyrexTypes.reduce_spanning_types(\n-            # Unpack the Python types to optimise and avoid a mix of inferred C and Python.\n+        # Unpack the Python types to optimise and avoid a mix of inferred C and Python.\n+        item_types = {\n             item_type.equivalent_type if item_type.is_pyobject and item_type.equivalent_type else item_type\n             for item_type in item_types\n-        )\n-        if item_type is py_object_type:\n-            # Normalise \"cannot infer anything specific\" to \"cannot infer\".\n+        }\n+        if len(item_types) != 1:\n+            # Only infer an item type if all items have the same type.  Otherwise,\n+            # converting the items to the inferred type may change their type or\n+            # value, e.g. when mixing bool with int or int with float.\n             return None",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/8114#discussion_r4478829013",
