            "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/commits/9ba7db36bdd4c7046211de0ee6f251dcc4f7e47d/comments",
            "commit": {
                "author": {
                    "date": "2026-11-04T13:18:57Z",
                    "email": "148060537+akasakariko@users.noreply.github.com",
                    "name": "akasakariko"
                },
                "comment_count": 0,
                "committer": {
                    "date": "2026-11-04T13:18:57Z",
                    "email": "148060537+akasakariko@users.noreply.github.com",
                    "name": "akasakariko"
                },
                "message": "Fix type inference for iteration over literal sequences with mixed item types (GH-8103)\n\nIterating over a literal sequence whose items have different types, such as\n(123, 123.45) or [True, 2], could coerce all items to a common C type and\nchange the type or value of the loop variable.  Single-character bytes\nliterals were inferred as C characters, so looping over [b'a', b'b'] produced\nintegers instead of bytes objects.\n\nOnly infer an item type if all items have the same type and keep\nsingle-character bytes literals as bytes objects.  Single-character string\nliterals still iterate over Py_UCS4, which converts back to str.",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "fdfef0fb226eb4ac8faeb59ad6d276fcdd2ee2c9",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/trees/fdfef0fb226eb4ac8faeb59ad6d276fcdd2ee2c9"
                },
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/commits/9ba7db36bdd4c7046211de0ee6f251dcc4f7e47d",
                "verification": {
                    "payload": "tree fdfef0fb226eb4ac8faeb59ad6d276fcdd2ee2c9\nparent 7b3aab3633c00a8e05f2e2ff13c044bd91ccb1ed\nauthor akasakariko <148060537+akasakariko@users.noreply.github.com> 1793798337 +0900\ncommitter akasakariko <148060537+akasakariko@users.noreply.github.com> 1793798337 +0900\n\nFix type inference for iteration over literal sequences with mixed item types (GH-8103)\n\nIterating over a literal sequence whose items have different types, such as\n(123, 123.45) or [True, 2], could coerce all items to a common C type and\nchange the type or value of the loop variable.  Single-character bytes\nliterals were inferred as C characters, so looping over [b'a', b'b'] produced\nintegers instead of bytes objects.\n\nOnly infer an item type if all items have the same type and keep\nsingle-character bytes literals as bytes objects.  Single-character string\nliterals still iterate over Py_UCS4, which converts back to str.\n",
                    "reason": "valid",
                    "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgHoPlOv56eGfsubbyfuXizxPx9v\nooCr4Kpg/3lmawcS8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGOMTpjT69oa3PHuAhXAc82dxangM5oJ7oxg/6G1SkQlLShun/v8KR1aBNyd0qYXdx\nk3P9pO92SZSAsv+JctwAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----",
                    "verified": true,
