                "comment_count": 0,
                "committer": {
                    "date": "2026-11-05T10:10:18Z",
                    "email": "Kayano04@outlook.jp",
                    "name": "KayanoLiam"
                },
                "message": "Avoid changing Python value types when reducing sequence item types\n\nReducing item types of mixed literal sequences should not convert values\nto a different Python type.  Move the check into reduce_spanning_types()\nand fall back to a generic object type if the spanning type would change\nthe Python type of any of the values, e.g. int -> float, bool -> int or\nfloat -> complex.  C integer and floating point types can still be widened\nwithin their value type, e.g. int -> long.\n\nMove the single-character bytes iteration fix to a separate PR, as\nsuggested in review.\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "0dd88964ccd58fb2ea18fad88693e7e3213a3f5a",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/git/trees/0dd88964ccd58fb2ea18fad88693e7e3213a3f5a"
